  "verbalization": "Oscillamide C is shown to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a known target of multiple compounds, including (+)-Phylliroside, quillaic acid, and Dimethyl 3-hydroxyphthalate. These compounds all share a common target of the histone methyltransferase enzyme, Histone-lysine N-methyltransferase, H3 lysine-9 specific 5. The evidence suggests that Oscillamide C may exert its biological effects through a mechanism that involves the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2). This implies that Oscillamide C could act as a modulator of the PRC2 complex, potentially influencing histone methylation at lysine 9 of histone H3. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a strong and reliable relationship between Oscillamide C and the target enzyme, supported by multiple independent targets that converge on the same molecular pathway. The mechanism appears to be mechanistically coherent, with Oscillamide C acting through a shared target complex that is also targeted by other compounds, suggesting a potential role in epigenetic regulation.",
